  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="They Killed the Father!" id="a74c-b16d-6804-ced3" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Magus and Patriarch are both killed, at the moment the last has died all Brood Brother units and Hybrid Broods must take a Morale test with the following modifiers: -1 if the unit is &lt; 50% starting strength and -1 if the unit is pinned or falling back. If this test is passed, the unit is Fearless for the rest of the game. If it failed, the unit will Fall Back immediately, though they can regroup in later turns as normal.

If the unit was in combat when this Fall Back move occurs, the enemy unit may only Consolidate.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Our Father Watches Us, Let None Fail Him!" id="263b-0275-dacc-4238" hidden="false">
      <description>All Brood Brother units with a model within 12&quot; of the Magus or Patriarch count as having Leadership 10 for all Morale checks and tests to Regroup. These units can still test to Regroup, even if they are below 50% of starting strength or within 6&quot; of an enemy unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Poor Maintenance" id="7b06-16e4-067d-a5f5" hidden="false">
      <description>After moving a Cult vehicle in the movement phase roll 2D6. On a roll of 2, the vehicle is immobilised the rest of the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hypnotic Gaze" id="7480-6633-9906-f11b" hidden="false">
      <description>Use during any Assault Phase after all models have moved but before any combat takes place. If the Cult psyker passes the Psychic Test, choose an enemy model in base contact. That model will need to roll 6&apos;s to hit in Assault that round. If the Psychic Test was successful, and the roll was higher than the enemy model&apos;s leadership, then the enemy cannot strike any blows at all.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rending Claws" id="b3e6-8d18-5e36-d27e" hidden="false">
      <description>Any attacks which roll a 6 to hit wound automatically and ignore armour saves. When rolling to penetrate vehicle armour, if a 6 is rolled then the user can add an additional D6 to the score.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Firebombs" id="df64-e7af-188e-83b3" hidden="false">
      <description>Firebombs work exactly like Frag Grenades, but prevent any assaulting Cultists from advancing. Any cult units involved in the assault may only consolidate. They also can only be used once per game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cult Relic" id="c8e6-e2a6-e887-5a21" hidden="false">
      <description>If a unit carrying this Relic has just failed a Morale test and is falling back, after the Fall Back movement is resolved (but before the enemy decides to Consolidate or Pursue) it can take another Morale test to Regroup. Normal restrictions for Regrouping apply.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Genestealer Magus" id="c406-23d3-1c02-6e7f" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="40"/>
      </costs>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink name="Genestealer Cult Armoury" id="d4a3-d58e-cc88-944f" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" targetId="1009-6cf9-3398-f840" type="selectionEntryGroup"/>
      </entryLinks>
